gin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $W,$ and the vector $b$ above. If the normal equation for the corresponding weighted least-squares problem $W\\,Ax=Wb$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 7 \\\\ 7 & b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518129 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4429ddaa-a525-58c0-92b3-0e53fe11c811" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518129 #edb/ref 1074 "To get the normal equation corresponding to $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ we pre-multiply both sides of the equation by $(W\\,A)^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot W\\,Ax & =(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot Wb \\\\ {A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)Ax & ={A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n{W}^{T}W=[\\begin{aligned}{1}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {3}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {2}^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nour normal equation can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 9 \\\\ 4 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}14 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 17\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=14+17+(-11)=20.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518291 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186518292 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518291 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bfe95e7b-6300-507c-9c3b-ebf83c2fe680" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518291 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186162356 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518292 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186518300 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518292 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c33819f8-c46b-5dee-a664-df0a06fddca7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518292 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186363141 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518297 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186518304 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518297 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cfea7d4a-7abe-545a-885a-a12f28682791" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518297 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186269157 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518300 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186518297 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518300 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d69dbc57-2846-5307-b0ec-b87f9e963a12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518300 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186269156 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518304 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "dbe4af0f-6deb-5714-9b84-7310ef2b54a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518304 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186518129 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
